\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces Runge oscillatory ringing induced by cubic polynomial detrending on Decca \textit  {et al.}\ (2003) Fig.~4(b) residuals ($N = 497$). Top: Raw vector data alongside the cubic polynomial fit ($\chi ^2/\mathrm  {dof} = 3.74$) and the physical inverse-power basis ($\chi ^2/\mathrm  {dof} = 1.14$). Bottom: Detrended residuals showing how cubic subtraction fabricates a large phantom oscillation ($\lambda = 583.5\,\mathrm  {nm}$, $\mathrm  {FAP} = 1.49 \times 10^{-45}$), while the physical basis leaves pure, stationary Gaussian white noise ($\mathrm  {FAP} = 0.163$).}}{6}{figure.2.1}\protected@file@percent }
