\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.2}{\ignorespaces High-frequency attenuation induced by cubic spline resampling on the irregular coordinate grid of Decca \textit  {et al.}\ Fig.~3(b) ($\mathrm  {CV}(\Delta z) = 40.7\%$). Top: An injected high-frequency oscillation ($\lambda = 7.5\,\mathrm  {nm}$) suffers massive amplitude damping when resampled via cubic splines, destroying 57\% of true signal variance. Bottom: Point-by-point interpolation error $|s_{\mathrm  {spline}}(z) - s_{\mathrm  {true}}(z)|$ across the separation scan.}}{8}{figure.2.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spline_attenuation}{{2.2}{8}{High-frequency attenuation induced by cubic spline resampling on the irregular coordinate grid of Decca \textit {et al.}\ Fig.~3(b) ($\mathrm {CV}(\Delta z) = 40.7\%$). Top: An injected high-frequency oscillation ($\lambda = 7.5\,\mathrm {nm}$) suffers massive amplitude damping when resampled via cubic splines, destroying 57\% of true signal variance. Bottom: Point-by-point interpolation error $|s_{\mathrm {spline}}(z) - s_{\mathrm {true}}(z)|$ across the separation scan}{figure.2.2}{}}
